          Question
Following a security audit, the xFusionCorp Industries security team has opted to enhance application and server security with SELinux. To initiate testing, the following requirements have been established for App server 1 in the Stratos Datacenter:
1-Install the required SELinux packages.
2-Permanently disable SELinux for the time being; it will be re-enabled after necessary configuration changes.
3-No need to reboot the server, as a scheduled maintenance reboot is already planned for tonight.
4-Disregard the current status of SELinux via the command line; the final status after the reboot should be disabled.

             Solution
1-Login into app server 1
   ssh tony@stapp01
 -Install SELinux Packages
 On RHEL/CentOS/Fedora-based systems:
   sudo yum install -y selinux-policy selinux-policy-targeted policycoreutils policycoreutils-python-utils libselinux-utils
 On Debian/Ubuntu-based systems:
   sudo apt update
   sudo apt install -y selinux-basics selinux-policy-default auditd
2-Permanently Disable SELinux
 Edit the configuration file:
    sudo vi /etc/selinux/config
 Set the following values:
    SELINUX=disabled
    SELINUXTYPE=targeted
 save and exitr
3-Confirm Configuration
 Check the file contents:
    grep SELINUX /etc/selinux/config
 Expected output:
   SELINUX=disabled
   SELINUXTYPE=targeted
